 "_about": "How the launch pair's parked waves play in a live match (docs/animation/pair-live.md). aliases: other names for a fighter of fighters.json (the neutral id rival is the antihero). A roster id is mapped to a fighter of data/anim/fighters.json (its key, or the id it `replaces`: KAI is the protagonist, VORR the antihero), whose waves are baked when his first body is built. shared: waves baked for both. gated: a strike that joins its fighter's pick list only while its gate is open (both_ground: both fighters near the ground; striker_air: the striker well above it); the other strikes of his strike waves (the manifest's light and heavy ones, never the tail) are the pick lists, walked as the go-live step 1 lists are. kinds: a shot kind (data/fight/shots.json) to the energy role it plays. cues: the sim's render cues (SimFx.cue) to what they start. spray_gap: ticks between a fighter's bolts under which the next one is a spray beat (the spread window of agency-pass.md 15.4). roles: per fighter, what each role plays: seq (a sequence of a parked wave, started where the cue or the shot says), hold (a pose held and eased: ticks, in and out seconds, w the weight), charged (charge: the pose held from the charge cue, full: the pose it takes at the flash, release: the hold on the shot), taunts (the far taunts: one is picked by a hash of the tick), taunt_first (the gesture a stand-off opens with, before any blow has landed), taunt_close, taunt_close_air (the close taunt when he is in the air), drop_the_act, crown_release, shove (events the sim does not send yet: they play when it does). Render only, outside the sim's data hash. gesture_groups: the groups of bones an intro gesture plays on (head, torso, arms, legs). roles.<fighter>.gestures: for each of Narrative's ten gesture intents (docs/narrative/dynamic-intros.md section 11) the fighter's own small motion: seq (a sequence or a pose id), w (a weight, optional), mask (the groups it plays on, default head, torso and arms), hold (seconds, for a pose). An intent a fighter has no entry for plays nothing. Started by the sim's `intro_gesture {actor, intent, at}` (the intent in `kind`, the point in `text`).",
